```sql
--Description:
--Step-by-step thinking inside one query:
--1.  Locate every person whose name text contains “Shahrukh” (case-insensitive pattern match).
--2.  Join those people to the movie-cast table on PID.  TRIM() is applied on both sides because
--    many PID values in the raw tables start with a space, which otherwise prevents matching.
--3.  Select each distinct movie ID (MID) that results from this join.
--4.  Limit output to 20 rows so we can quickly inspect that the join really worked.
SELECT DISTINCT mc."MID"
FROM "Person"  AS p
JOIN "M_Cast" AS mc
     ON TRIM(p."PID") = TRIM(mc."PID")
WHERE p."Name" LIKE '%Shahrukh%'
LIMIT 20;
```
